docx4j
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

export-fo-x is a fork of docx4j-export-fo 11.5.9 and contains source code from
that project, both verbatim and modified.

    docx4j
    Copyright Plutext Pty Ltd
    https://www.docx4java.org/
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Of the 31 source files taken from docx4j-export-fo 11.5.9, 23 are unchanged and
8 were modified. Each modified file carries a notice to that effect in its
header, as required by section 4(b) of the Apache License. The eight are:

    org/docx4j/convert/out/fo/AbstractFOExporter.java
    org/docx4j/convert/out/fo/FOConversionImageHandler.java
    org/docx4j/convert/out/fo/FOPAreaTreeHelper.java
    org/docx4j/convert/out/fo/FOPictWriterAbstract.java
    org/docx4j/convert/out/fo/FOPictWriterFloatAvoided.java
    org/docx4j/convert/out/fo/FOPictWriterFloatUsed.java
    org/docx4j/convert/out/fo/FOPictWriterNoWrapImpl.java
    org/docx4j/convert/out/fo/docx2fo.xslt

Files under org/docx4j/convert/out/fo/x/ are new work by the export-fo-x
project. They sit in the docx4j package namespace on purpose: export-fo-x
is a drop-in replacement for docx4j-export-fo, so it has to keep that project's
package and resource names for Docx4J.toPDF to keep working unchanged.

